# Video calling off, so VoLTE survives a dropped IMS connection.
# With persist.vendor.vilte_support or persist.vendor.viwifi_support at 1 (the stock vendor's
# values), MediaTek's ImsService passes each new IMS network to its video telephony library, which
# waits for the media.VTS service. Stock's /system_ext/bin/vtservice provides it; this tree doesn't
# ship it, so the call never returns. It blocks ImsService's ConnectivityThread, the thread that
# delivers all its network callbacks: ImsService never hears that the IMS network was lost, stays
# in DisconnectingState, and the modem never asks for the IMS connection again. VoLTE is then down
# until a restart, after the first airplane mode toggle or network-side drop.
# Both are persist. properties, so the 0 is saved in /data. Deleting this file won't bring back 1:
# a change that enables ViLTE later (by shipping vtservice) has to set 1 itself.
on property:persist.vendor.vilte_support=1
    setprop persist.vendor.vilte_support 0

on property:persist.vendor.viwifi_support=1
    setprop persist.vendor.viwifi_support 0
